<h2>How much do full-arch dental implants cost?</h2>
<p>A responsible estimate starts with a defined treatment plan. Cost may change based on:</p>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>One arch or both upper and lower arches</li>
  <li>The planned number and type of implants</li>
  <li>Extractions, bone grafting, or staged treatment</li>
  <li>Imaging, sedation, and surgical complexity</li>
  <li>Provisional and final restoration design and materials</li>
  <li>Individual maintenance and follow-up needs</li>
</ul>
<p>Coverage varies by insurance plan. The practice can help review available benefits, but no benefit or financing approval is guaranteed. Current site information identifies Cherry financing and in-house payment plans; terms and approval depend on the applicable program.</p>
<p>For a deeper explanation, read <a href="/blog/full-mouth-implant-cost-arizona/" data-action="implant-financing" data-position="financing">what changes the cost of full-mouth implants</a> and visit our <a href="/insurance-financing/?source=full-arch" data-action="implant-financing" data-position="financing">insurance and financing page</a>.</p>
